[3] COHESIVE ENERGY RESULTS
------------------------------------------------------------
Sum of isolated atoms   :  -348.563635 eV
Bulk structure energy   :  -364.562158 eV

Cohesive energy = (Bulk structure energy - Sum of isolated atoms) / Total atoms. More negative means a more strongly bound structure. 'Delta vs Uncorrected' isolates the effect of each correction alone on the final per-atom result.
Method         | Total (eV) | Per atom (eV/atom) | Delta vs Uncorrected (eV/atom)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Uncorrected    | -15.9985   | -7.9993            | (reference)                   
BSSE-corrected | -14.0607   | -7.0304            | +0.9689                       
BSSE correction per atom: +0.9689 eV/atom (uncorrected LCAO cohesive energies systematically over-bind -- expect this to make the energy less negative)

[3b] BSSE CUTOFF CONVERGENCE SCAN
------------------------------------------------------------
Cohesive energy per atom (BSSE-corrected) at each scanned cutoff -- from stb-cohesive's --bsse-convergence-increment given multiple values. The correction is converged once these stop changing appreciably as the cutoff grows; if it's still trending by the last point, increase --bsse-cutoff/--bsse-convergence-increment further.
Cutoff         | Per atom (eV/atom) | Delta vs base BSSE (eV/atom)
------------------------------------------------------------------
4.0 Ang (base) | -7.0304            | (reference)                 
6.0 Ang        | -7.0119            | +0.0185                     
8.0 Ang        | -7.0093            | +0.0210                     
10.0 Ang       | -7.0089            | +0.0215                     
Last step change: +0.0005 eV/atom (cutoff 8.0 -> 10.0 Ang) -- small means converged, large means keep increasing the cutoff.

